 # Preact Signals Rule

## Description
Enforces using `useSignal` instead of `signal` inside Preact components. This ensures proper component lifecycle management and state isolation.


## Message
Use useSignal() instead of signal() inside Preact components

## Severity
warning

## Check
```typescript
(context) => {
    // Only check inside .tsx files
    if (!context.filePath.endsWith('.tsx')) {
        return false;
    }

    // Get the file content
    const content = context.getFileContent();
    
    // Check if we're inside a component (function that returns JSX)
    const isInsideComponent = /function\s+\w+\s*\([^)]*\)\s*:\s*JSX\.Element\s*{/.test(content);
    
    // Check if we're inside a component (arrow function that returns JSX)
    const isInsideArrowComponent = /const\s+\w+\s*=\s*\([^)]*\)\s*:\s*JSX\.Element\s*=>\s*{/.test(content);
    
    // If we're inside a component and find signal(), trigger the rule
    return (isInsideComponent || isInsideArrowComponent) && /signal\(/.test(content);
}
```

## Fix
```typescript
(context) => {
    // Replace signal() with useSignal()
    return context.replace(/signal\(/g, 'useSignal(');
}
```

## Examples

### ❌ Bad
```typescript
function MyComponent(): JSX.Element {
    const count = signal(0);  // Using signal() inside component
    return <div>{count.value}</div>;
}
```

### ✅ Good
```typescript
function MyComponent(): JSX.Element {
    const count = useSignal(0);  // Using useSignal() inside component
    return <div>{count.value}</div>;
}
```

## When to use `signal` instead

Use `signal()` (not `useSignal()`) for:
- Global state
- State shared between components
- State outside of components
- Utility functions
- Services
- Store implementations

## Caveats

### ❌ Bad
```ts
// const menuState = { ..., currentScreen: signal(...) }

export function Menu(): JSX.Element {
    const currentScreen = useSignal(menuState.currentScreen.value); // useSignal and subscription is unecessary

    // Subscribe to menuState changes
    menuState.currentScreen.subscribe((newScreen) => {
        currentScreen.value = newScreen;
    });

    switch (currentScreen.value) {
        case 'about':
            return <AboutScreen />;
        case 'main-menu':
            return <MainMenuScreen />;
        default:
            return <MainMenuScreen />;
    }
}
```


### ✅ Good
```ts
export function Menu(): JSX.Element {
    switch (menuState.currentScreen.value) { /// using it like this just works
        case 'about':
            return <AboutScreen />;
        case 'main-menu':
            return <MainMenuScreen />;
        default:
            return <MainMenuScreen />;
    }
}
```

